# Aura Project Rules (UE 5.7)

This is an Unreal Engine **5.7** C++ project built around the **Gameplay Ability System (GAS)**, **Enhanced Input**, and a custom **WidgetController** UI pattern. Follow all conventions below when generating or editing code.

**Project facts (engine, plugins, class names):** `AGENTS.md` and `.agents/ue-project-context.md` — do not duplicate here.

---

## 1. Engine & Module

- Target engine: **Unreal Engine 5.7**. Do not target 5.2-era APIs or workarounds superseded in later versions.
- `Aura.Target.cs` / `AuraEditor.Target.cs` use `BuildSettingsVersion.V6` and `IncludeOrderVersion.Latest`.
- Primary game module: `Aura` (see `Source/Aura/Aura.Build.cs`).
- Public dependencies already wired: `Core`, `CoreUObject`, `Engine`, `InputCore`, `EnhancedInput`, `GameplayAbilities`, `UMG`.
- Private dependencies: `GameplayTags`, `GameplayTasks`, `NavigationSystem`, `Niagara`, `AIModule`.
- If new functionality needs another module (e.g. `Slate`, `OnlineSubsystem`), add it to `Aura.Build.cs` explicitly and mention it in the response.
- Editor automation: use **UEC MCP** (`uecp-aura`) for blueprints/assets/levels; C++ stays in Cursor.

## 2. File Layout

```
Source/Aura/
  Public/
    AbilitySystem/
      Abilities/          AuraGameplayAbility, AuraProjectileSpell, ...
      AbilityTasks/       TargetDataUnderMouse, ...
      Data/               AttributeInfo, ...
      ModMagCalc/         MMC_MaxHealth, MMC_MaxMana
      AuraAbilitySystemComponent.h
      AuraAttributeSet.h
      AuraAbilitySystemLibrary.h
    Actor/                AuraProjectile, AuraEffectActor
    Character/            CharacterBase, AuraCharacter, Enemy
    Game/                 AuraGameModeBase
    HUD/                  AuraHUD
    Input/                AuraInputComponent, AuraInputConfig
    Interaction/          CombatInterface, EnemyInterface
    Player/               AuraPlayerController, AuraPlayerState
    UI/
      Widget/             AuraUserWidget, ...
      WidgetController/   AuraWidgetController, OverlayWidgetController, AttributeMenuWidgetController
    AuraAssetManager.h
    AuraGameplayTags.h
  Private/                mirrors Public/
```

- New classes must be placed in the matching subfolder. `.h` in `Public/<dir>/`, `.cpp` in `Private/<dir>/`.
- One UCLASS per file. Filename matches class name without the prefix (`UAuraAttributeSet` -> `AuraAttributeSet.h/.cpp`).

## 3. Naming Conventions

- `A` prefix: Actors (`AAuraCharacter`, `AAuraProjectile`).
- `U` prefix: UObjects / components (`UAuraAbilitySystemComponent`, `UAuraUserWidget`).
- `F` prefix: structs (`FGameplayTagContainer`, `FEffectProperties`).
- `E` prefix: enums (`EAuraAbilityType`).
- `I` prefix: interfaces (`ICombatInterface`, `IEnemyInterface`).
- Project-specific prefixes for assets / classes (already in use):
  - `Aura...` for engine extensions (`UAuraAttributeSet`).
  - `GA_` Blueprint Gameplay Abilities, `GE_` Gameplay Effects, `MMC_` Modifier Magnitude Calculations.
  - `IA_` Input Actions, `IMC_` Input Mapping Contexts, `DA_` Data Assets.
  - `BP_` Blueprints, `WBP_` Widget Blueprints, `AM_` Anim Montages, `AN_` Anim Notifies.

## 4. C++ Style

- `#pragma once` at the top of every header.
- IWYU-compliant includes. The **first include** of any `.cpp` is its own header. Then minimal specific headers — not umbrella includes.
- Use `UPROPERTY()` / `UFUNCTION()` for any member that needs reflection, replication, GC tracking, or BP exposure.
- For UObject pointer members in UCLASSes, prefer `TObjectPtr<T>` over raw `T*`.
- No narrative comments. Comments only when intent is non-obvious.
- Prefer `UE_LOG` with a project log category over `GEngine->AddOnScreenDebugMessage` except for transient debug.

## 5. UE 5.7 API Notes (upgraded from 5.2)

- `FOverlapResult`: include `Engine/OverlapResult.h` when calling methods on overlap results (forward declare is insufficient in 5.7).
- `FGameplayAbilitySpec`: use `GetDynamicSpecSourceTags()` instead of deprecated `DynamicAbilityTags`.
- `FAuraGameplayEffectContext`: `GetScriptStruct()` must return `FAuraGameplayEffectContext::StaticStruct()`; `Duplicate()` must allocate `FAuraGameplayEffectContext`.
- Do not put `FGameplayEffectSpec` in `UFUNCTION(Client, Reliable)` RPCs — pass `FGameplayTagContainer` or other lightweight types.
- `AActor::NetUpdateFrequency`: prefer `SetNetUpdateFrequency()` / `GetNetUpdateFrequency()` over direct member access.
- `UAbilitySystemGlobals::InitGlobalData()` is called automatically from 5.3+; keep the call in `UAuraAssetManager` for clarity but it is not the 5.2-era manual requirement.

## 6. Gameplay Ability System (GAS)

- Attribute setters/getters: use `ATTRIBUTE_ACCESSORS` or GAS macros from `AttributeSet.h`.
- Always declare `FGameplayAttributeData` with `ReplicatedUsing = OnRep_<Name>` and `GAMEPLAYATTRIBUTE_REPNOTIFY` in `OnRep_<Name>`.
- Register replicated attributes in `GetLifetimeReplicatedProps` with `DOREPLIFETIME_CONDITION_NOTIFY(..., COND_None, REPNOTIFY_Always)`.
- New attributes must be added to `UAuraAttributeSet` and surfaced through `AttributeInfo` data assets for the UI menu.
- Gameplay Abilities inherit from `UAuraGameplayAbility`. Projectile spells inherit from `UAuraProjectileSpell`.
- Gameplay Effects: prefer Blueprint authoring under `Content/Blueprints/AbilitySystem/GameplayEffects/`.
- Use `FGameplayTag` everywhere. Native tags in `AuraGameplayTags.h/.cpp` via `FAuraGameplayTags::InitializeNativeGameplayTags()`.
- Ability tasks live under `AbilitySystem/AbilityTasks/`. Follow the `TargetDataUnderMouse` pattern.

## 7. Enhanced Input

- Input is driven by `IA_*` + `IMC_AuraContext` + `DA_AuraInputConfig`.
- Bindings happen in `UAuraInputComponent::BindAbilityActions(...)` — do not add per-action `BindAction` in the PlayerController.

## 8. UI (WidgetController pattern)

- Widgets (`UAuraUserWidget` and children) are **passive** — they never read game state directly.
- WidgetControllers sit between widget and model; widgets bind to controller delegates only.

## 9. Combat / Interfaces

- Cross-class combat goes through `ICombatInterface` and `IEnemyInterface`.
- Implement interfaces rather than `Cast<>` to concrete enemy/player types.

## 10. Replication & Networking

- `AbilitySystemComponent` on `APlayerState` for player, on pawn for `AEnemy`.
- Default spell policy: `LocalPredicted`. Use `WaitTargetData` / `TargetDataUnderMouse` for targeting.
- Replicated UPROPERTYs need `Replicated` (or `ReplicatedUsing=`) plus `DOREPLIFETIME`.

## 11. Assets & Async Loading

- Custom asset manager: `UAuraAssetManager` (set in `Config/DefaultEngine.ini`).
- Native gameplay tags bootstrapped in `UAuraAssetManager::StartInitialLoading()`.
- Prefer `UDataAsset` subclasses with `TObjectPtr<>` rather than hard string paths.

## 12. Niagara / VFX

- Niagara only — no Cascade. Trigger hit VFX via `GameplayCue` when possible.

## 13. What NOT to Do

- Do NOT use `ue-mcp` / third-party UE MCP — UEC (`uecp-aura`) is the editor bridge.
- Do NOT add Blueprint-only logic in C++ without `UFUNCTION(BlueprintCallable/BlueprintImplementableEvent)`.
- Do NOT use `TWeakObjectPtr` for normal owning references.
- Do NOT spawn projectiles via raw `SpawnActor` from abilities — use `UAuraProjectileSpell::SpawnProjectile`.
- Do NOT hardcode key bindings — use `IMC_AuraContext` + `DA_AuraInputConfig`.
- Do NOT include private GAS module headers; use public headers only.

## 14. When in Doubt

- Read the closest existing class first and mirror its style.
- For GAS: defer to `AuraAttributeSet.cpp`, `AuraAbilitySystemComponent.cpp`, `AuraProjectileSpell.cpp`.
- For UI: defer to `OverlayWidgetController.cpp` / `AttributeMenuWidgetController.cpp`.

